method.description:
Registers a [Callable] that is invoked after every CPU memory write ([code]MREQ + WR[/code]). Signature: [code]func(addr: int, value: int) -> void[/code].
[br][br]The write to internal RAM has already been applied when the callback fires. Use this to implement memory mappers that trap writes to specific address ranges (e.g. MegaROM bankswitching, RAM mirroring, or memory-mapped peripherals).
[br][br][b]Konami4 (K4) MegaROM example:[/b]
[codeblock]
func _ready():
    cpu.set_mem_write_callback(Callable(self, "_on_mem_write"))

func _on_mem_write(addr: int, val: int) -> void:
    if addr >= 0x6000 and addr <= 0x7FFF:
        _k4_map_segment(0x6000, val)  # switch page 1
    elif addr >= 0x8000 and addr <= 0x9FFF:
        _k4_map_segment(0x8000, val)  # switch page 2
    elif addr >= 0xA000 and addr <= 0xBFFF:
        _k4_map_segment(0xA000, val)  # switch page 3
[/codeblock]
[b]Note:[/b] This callback is called on every memory write and must execute quickly to avoid stalling the emulation loop.
